config DRM_SPRD_GSP
	tristate "SPRD DRM GSP driver"
	depends on ARCH_SPRD
	depends on DRM_SPRD
	depends on SPRD_IOMMU
	help
	  GSP is hardware which not only can compose multiple layers
	  but also can transform and scale layers.

	  The T618 is a "pike2" part and binds to the
	  "sprd,gsp-lite_r2p0-pike2" compatible string, which selects
	  the gsp_lite_r2p0 core.

	  Note: the gsp_layer buffer path calls the Unisoc ION helper
	  sprd_ion_is_reserved(). ION was dropped from mainline and no
	  provider for that symbol exists in this tree or in any donor, so
	  gsp_ion_stub.c supplies it as a documented shim that always reports
	  "not reserved", which puts the caller on the IOVA path. The other
	  helper gsp_layer.c calls, sprd_ion_get_phys_addr(), comes from the
	  real ported driver in drivers/dma-buf/sprd/ and is deliberately not
	  duplicated here. The module links, loads and probes; a layer whose
	  buffer really is a reserved ION carveout will take the IOVA path,
	  which is a functional limitation rather than a memory-safety one.

config DRM_SPRD_GSP_IPC_TRUSTY
	bool "SPRD DRM GSP widevine driver"
	depends on DRM_SPRD_GSP
	depends on TRUSTY_VIRTIO_IPC
	help
	  This function is to support the widevine function.

config DRM_SPRD_GSP_DVFS
	bool "SPRD DRM GSP dvfs driver"
	depends on DRM_SPRD_GSP
	depends on SPRD_APSYS_DVFS
	help
	  This function is to support the dvfs function.
